  "body": "[RFC 4329](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4329) deprecated all `text` JavaScript types, so that should probably be mentioned in the specification (but they still have to be parsed as valid JavaScript types, as legacy websites tend to use `type/javascript`).\r\n\r\nThis probably also applies to `application/x-javascript` and `application/x-ecmascript`, as they use the `x-` prefix, usage of which is deprecated according to [RFC 6838](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6838).",
